														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843045">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, Comedy.</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional):</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
A human skull that becomes sentient at a random point one day every week, with a friendly over dramatic demeanor, interested in nothing but bones. Knowledge of the entity was found by the foundation when reports of a skull, sitting atop piles of human/animal flesh was found. this scp has the ability of weak hypnosis over individuals to bring it desired bones, and an interest in the foundation itself, constantly going through classified files while just saying it wants to get to know the place.</p>
<ul>
<li>list item</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> After being put into foundation containment, scp-5212 awakes and then tries to strike up a conversation with researches working on it, it takes a liking to one researcher &quot;Dr. Atlas&quot; who conducts most of the interviews on the entity, and experiences scp-5212's ability to get whatever he wants from anyone he wants, using hypnosis (but while thinking they're just really good at convincing) after SCP-5212 gains access to highly classified information, Dr Atlas is terminated by higher up for failure to properly secure foundation secrets, and is replaced by &quot;Dr. B&quot; who scp-5212 eventually deals with.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> the entity has a mysterious personality and power, you don't know if its entertaining and fun demeanor is an act or not, or even if its from our own reality or just an explorer, the exact character of the skull is strange, and almost creepy in a way.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> scp-5212 is heavily story driven through its interviews and post interview report logs.</p>

