<p>Assuming that the battery hold enough energy for India's consumption, this is actually not as bad as you estimated.</p>
<p>[In case you're curious, India has had 720 capital deaths since 1947. Also, given that The Foundation goes through 3K+ D-Class annually, this isn't as bad as you think.]</p>
<p>2) This also keeps it out of the political/targeted area. This makes essentially fodder for questioning what a government is willing to do for its people, and what those people are willing to ignore if it's to their benefit.</p>
<p>3) It feels weird that it has a Latin name given it's an Indian anomaly. Just sayin'.</p>
<p>4) Overall, it's not a bad concept and allows for some pretty good political commentary.</p>

